minimax-code2api
================

This project contains code adapted from the following third-party sources:

1. MiniMax-AI/minimax-code (https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code)
   - File: packages/oauth-lease-protocol/src/{contracts.ts, codec.ts, endpoints.ts}
   - Adapted into: src/lease.js
   - Copyright (c) 2026 MiniMax Code
   - License: MIT (https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code/blob/main/LICENSE)
   - Changes: ported from TypeScript to plain JavaScript; trimmed to the
     client-side subset (frame codec, endpoint resolution, protocol
     constants/error codes); server-side code and capability provisioning
     were removed.

2. Model metadata in src/models.js mirrors the first-run model catalog from
   MiniMax-AI/minimax-code (packages/config/src/minimax-model-catalog.ts),
   Copyright (c) 2026 MiniMax Code, MIT.

Design references (no code copied):
   - TriDefender/zcode-api — overall "coding-plan to API" proxy design
   - router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI — multi-protocol gateway layout
   - Wei-Shaw/sub2api — token/credential lifecycle handling

This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by MiniMax. It talks to the
locally installed MiniMax Code desktop app on the user's own machine, using
the desktop app's own local credential-leasing interface, and forwards
requests to MiniMax endpoints on behalf of that logged-in account. Use of the
underlying MiniMax service remains subject to MiniMax's terms of service.
